# Immediate GitHub Pages production deploy (primary)

This project opts into auto-deploy. After a task that changes files, ship to GitHub Pages **first**, **without asking**. Do not wait for "закоммить / запушь / задеплой".

GitHub Pages is the **primary** live host (Cargo iframe embed). Vercel is secondary — see `vercel-deploy.mdc`.

## One repo, all products

One Vite app, one GitHub Pages site (`fovkotov/kaik`). A single push to `main` updates every product:

| Product | URL path | Source |
|---|---|---|
| Site (course) | `/kaik/` | `index.html` |
| Admin | `/kaik/admin` | `admin.html` |
| Catalog | `/kaik/catalog` | `catalog.html` |

Do not treat them as separate apps. Do not skip a deploy because "only admin changed".

Live host: `https://fovkotov.github.io/kaik/`

## How it works

- Workflow: `.github/workflows/pages.yml`
- Trigger: every push to `main` (and manual `workflow_dispatch`)
- Build: `npm run build:pages` → `vite build --base /kaik/`
- Artifact: `dist/` with `.nojekyll` and `404.html` copy for SPA routing

## How to ship

When git is in use (normal case):

```bash
git push origin main
```

Commit first if the working tree has relevant changes — see `git-push.mdc`. The push triggers the Pages workflow automatically.

Local build check (optional, before push):

```bash
npm run build:pages
```

Force a redeploy without new commits (rare):

```bash
gh workflow run pages.yml
```

- Do not update git config. Do not commit secrets (`.env`, tokens).
- **Never** force-push.

## Deploy order after file changes

1. **Commit + push to GitHub** → GitHub Pages (primary)
2. **Vercel CLI deploy** → secondary mirror (`vercel-deploy.mdc`)

Wait for the Pages workflow to finish when possible:

```bash
gh run list --workflow=pages.yml --limit 1
gh run watch --exit-status
```

## After deploy

Reply with the three live URLs:

- https://fovkotov.github.io/kaik/
- https://fovkotov.github.io/kaik/admin
- https://fovkotov.github.io/kaik/catalog

Then the Vercel mirror URLs from `vercel-deploy.mdc`.
